<title>UK: UK's Brown says to address sterling concerns.</title>
<headline>UK's Brown says to address sterling concerns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said in his budget speech he shared industry concerns about sterling and will address them.</p>
<p>&quot;The current strength of sterling, over the last year, has appreciated by 18 percent. I understand and share the concerns of industry and exporters and will address them,&quot; Brown told parliament.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
